        <p class="article__lead reveal">Rwanda's nickname, <em>le pays des mille collines</em>, the land of a thousand hills, is no exaggeration. Almost every view is a sea of green ridges, terraced farms and tea estates folding into the distance. The scenery isn't a backdrop here; it's one of the great pleasures of the journey.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Why the thousand hills matter</h2>
        <p class="reveal">Rwanda is small, compact and almost entirely upland, which means short transfers and constantly beautiful drives. The hills are intensively, lovingly farmed, banana groves, terraces and some of the finest tea and coffee in Africa, and they make even the road between two parks an experience to savour.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Tea &amp; coffee country</h2>
        <p class="reveal">Rwanda's high altitude and volcanic soils produce exceptional coffee and tea, much of it grown by women's cooperatives. A washing station or tea estate tour, picking, processing and tasting, is a warm, hands on way to meet the people behind the cup and to support the communities who grow it.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Ways to enjoy the scenery</h2>
        <ul class="reveal">
          <li><strong>Scenic drives:</strong> the Congo Nile trail along Lake Kivu and the road to Nyungwe are among Africa's loveliest.</li>
          <li><strong>Gentle hikes:</strong> community guided walks through villages, terraces and tea fields, at any pace.</li>
          <li><strong>Cycling &amp; e bikes:</strong> a growing network of routes for keen riders, with options for all abilities.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="reveal">Best time to visit</h2>
        <p class="reveal">The hills are green year round, but views are clearest and trails driest in the <strong>June to September</strong> and <strong>December to February</strong> windows. The green seasons bring atmospheric mist and the deepest greens of all. See our <a href="best-time-rwanda.html">best time to visit Rwanda</a> guide for more.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Where it fits in your journey</h2>
        <p class="reveal">You'll experience the thousand hills on every transfer, but we also build in time to slow down and enjoy them, a tea estate lunch, a village walk, a sundowner over the ridges. They are the connecting thread between the gorillas, the forest, the savanna and the lake. We arrange it all, door to door.</p>

